  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Techincal advisors were placed in Kiribati as part of the Australia Pacific Partnerships Platform (AusP3) under the Kiribati Infrastructure investment. The role of Director of the National Economic and Planning Office was engaged through AusP3 to strengthen capacity and support improved public financial management and economic governance within the Ministry of Finance and Economic Development (MFED).  In 2023, the Director worked with the team and submitted cabinet papers on significant policy issues, including a debt sustainability policy paper and a fiscal strategy for the 2024 budget.  The Director also supported MFED in developing policies for private sector employees&apos; leave grants which involved data matching with other ministries to verify eligibility and ensure no duplication with other benefits.  A significant amount of duplication was identified, resulting in reduced costs of the program and assisting the Government of Kiribati with financial sustainability.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The recruitment and placement of technical advisors in Kiribati through the Australia Pacific Partnerships Platform (AusP3) is an agreement under the Kiribati Infrastructure investment.  The role of Director of Engineering Services was engaged through AusP3 to support the capacity of the Ministry of Infrastructure and Sustainable Energy (MISE) with the planning, design and delivery of climate resilient civil infrastructure projects, including the management of operations and maintenance of built assets. In the reporting period, the Director supported MISE to revise the Building Code to incorporate universal access as a key requirement of all building designs in Kiribati and facilitated the tabling of the revised Building Act and Building Code to Parliament.  As a result, accessibility audits have been conducted on numerous government buildings with multiple recommendations to improve accessibility to government offices and services for people with disabilities.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Australia Pacific Partnerships Platform (AusP3), Australia assisted the Ministry of Infrastructure and Sustainable Energy (MISE) to fund and recruit for a Director of Engineering Services. Over the last 12 months, the Director provided technical advice across all engineering departments, including civil and construction works, architecture and design and quality assurance. The Director also played a role in drafting cabinet papers, providing strategic planning and engaging in the development of infrastructure policies, as well as building the capacity of staff to strengthen the quality of infrastructure, which is vital in facilitating economic growth in the long-term.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
